DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iiwwmmbbttffww utility downloads the specified firmware file to the speci‐
     fied ugen(4) device.

     This utility will _o_n_l_y work with Intel Wireless 7260/8260/9260 chip based
     Bluetooth USB devices and some of their successors.  The identification
     is currently based on USB vendor ID/product ID pair.  The vendor ID
     should be 0x8087 (USB_VENDOR_INTEL2) and the product ID should be one of
     the supported devices.

     Firmware files are available in the _c_o_m_m_s_/_i_w_m_b_t_-_f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e port.

     The iiwwmmbbttffww utility will query the device to determine which firmware im‐
     age and board configuration to load in at runtime.

     The options are as follows:

     --II                Enable informational debugging.

     --DD                Enable verbose debugging.

     --dd _d_e_v_i_c_e___n_a_m_e    Specify ugen(4) device name.

     --ff _f_i_r_m_w_a_r_e___p_a_t_h  Specify the directory containing the firmware files to
                       search and upload.

     --hh                Display usage message and exit.

